        "provenance": "original",
        "title": {
          "en": "The treasure map"
        },
        "text": {
          "en": "A map has the school at (1, 2) and the temple at (7, 10). How far apart are they, and where is the point halfway? Coordinates answer both."
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "explain",
        "type": "explanation",
        "provenance": "original",
        "keepEnglishTerms": [
          "distance formula",
          "Pythagoras",
          "mid-point",
          "section formula",
          "trisection",
          "centroid"
        ],
        "text": {
          "en": "The distance between P(x1, y1) and Q(x2, y2) is the square root of [(x2 - x1) squared + (y2 - y1) squared].\nIt comes from Pythagoras theorem on a right triangle drawn between the points.\nThe mid-point of PQ is ((x1 + x2)/2, (y1 + y2)/2).\nThe point dividing PQ internally in the ratio m : n is ((m x2 + n x1)/(m + n), (m y2 + n y1)/(m + n)).\nThe points of trisection divide the segment in ratios 1 : 2 and 2 : 1.\nThe centroid of a triangle with vertices (x1,y1), (x2,y2), (x3,y3) is ((x1+x2+x3)/3, (y1+y2+y3)/3)."
        }
      },
